DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261013
SUMMARY:Deadline: Institute for Law & AI: Winter Research Fellowship EU Law
  2027 (Cambridge\, UK)
DESCRIPTION:The Institute for Law & AI's Winter Research Fellowship (EU Law
 ) is a 10-week full-time paid research fellowship for lawyers who want to 
 deepen their understanding of AI and law and contribute to the field\, wit
 h close support and mentorship from LawAI staff. Previous Seasonal Researc
 h Fellows have gone on to legal and policy roles in the European AI Office
 \, leading AI companies\, academia and think tanks\, including LawAI itsel
 f. FUNDING: a GBP 1\,000 weekly stipend plus a GBP 7\,000 relocation and h
 ousing payment\; fellows work from LawAI's Cambridge\, UK office\, with re
 mote candidates considered in exceptional circumstances. ELIGIBILITY: open
  to graduate law students\, professionals and academics with diverse skill
  sets\, experience levels and degrees of knowledge in AI law and policy. F
 ellowship runs 1 February to 9 April 2027. Applications are considered on 
 a rolling basis as received\, so apply early. DEADLINE: 12 October 2026.\n
 \nOrganisation: Institute for Law & AI (LawAI)\nLocation: Cambridge\, UK (
 in-office\; remote candidates considered in exceptional circumstances). GB
 P 7\,000 relocation and housing payment provided.\nAward: GBP 1\,000 weekl
 y stipend for the 10-week fellowship (GBP 10\,000 total)\, plus a GBP 7\,0
 00 relocation and housing payment. No application fee.\nDuration: 10 weeks
  full-time\, 1 February to 9 April 2027\, based at LawAI's Cambridge\, UK 
 office.\n\nMore: https://law-ai.org/wrf-eu/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://law-ai.org/wrf-eu/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_me
 dium=referral
LOCATION:Cambridge\, UK (in-office\; remote candidates considered in except
 ional circumstances). GBP 7\,000 relocation and housing payment provided.
END:VEVENT
