UID:braunschweig-projects-hbk-fellowships-2027-28@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20261104T144744Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261004
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261005
SUMMARY:Deadline: Braunschweig Projects 2027/28: Artistic Fellowships at HB
 K Braunschweig (Fine Arts and Sound Art)
DESCRIPTION:With Braunschweig Projects\, HBK Braunschweig (one of Germany's
  largest art academies\, with fine arts\, art education\, performing arts\
 , design\, visual communication\, art history and media studies) offers 7 
 artistic fellowships on behalf of the State of Lower Saxony for 2027/28: 5
  in fine arts and 2 in sound art. The programme promotes young artists and
  internationalisation\, and is aimed at artists who want to work on a proj
 ect in the immediate vicinity of HBK\; proposals should make a significant
  contribution to the further development of forms of artistic practice. Ea
 ch fellow is assigned a self-chosen mentor from the fine arts professors\,
  all professors of the fine arts department are available for artistic dis
 course\, and fellows can present their project's progress within the unive
 rsity. Fellows are expected to participate in the Welcome Weeks (19 to 30 
 April 2027) and a joint final presentation in January/February 2028\, and 
 must reside at HBK for at least 8 months during the summer and winter seme
 ster lecture periods. FUNDING: EUR 1\,600 per month for 12 months from 1 A
 pril 2027\, a rent-free one-person studio apartment (EUR 250 per month con
 tribution to incidental costs)\, and an allowance for project and travel c
 osts\; a short final report (about 1 page) is due at the end. ELIGIBILITY:
  a successfully completed art degree\, with the most recent studies comple
 ted after 31 March 2016 and before 1 April 2023\; proof of extensive artis
 tic practice and exhibition participation\; no regular third-party benefit
 s (salary\, work scholarships or state subsidy) during the funding period.
  APPLICATION: in German or English by email to application-bsprojects[at]h
 bk-bs.de\, addressed to President Prof. Dr. Ana Dimke\, with the completed
  and signed application form\, an artistic profile (one file\, max 15MB: n
 ame\, website and social media\, artist statement max 350 words\, project 
 description max 350 words\, portfolio of 10 to 15 works\, short CV\, links
  to 3 password-free video/audio files) and the diploma of the most recent 
 degree (PDF\, max 1MB). DEADLINE: 4 October 2026. A separate Braunschweig 
 Projects curatorial fellowship for 2027/28 runs in parallel.\n\nOrganisati
 on: Braunschweig University of Art (HBK Braunschweig)\, on behalf of the S
 tate of Lower Saxony\nLocation: Braunschweig\, Germany. Open international
 ly (application in German or English)\; fellows must reside at HBK for at 
 least 8 months during the lecture periods.\nAward: Stipend of EUR 1\,600 p
 er month for 12 months\, plus a rent-free one-person studio apartment in B
 raunschweig (fellows pay EUR 250 per month towards incidental living costs
 ) and an allowance for project and travel costs. 7 fellowships: 5 in fine 
 arts and 2 in sound art. No application fee.\nDuration: 12 months from 1 A
 pril 2027 (accommodation from 15 April 2027)\; Welcome Weeks 19 to 30 Apri
 l 2027\; joint final presentation January/February 2028\n\nMore: https://w
 ww.hbk-bs.de/hochschule/stipendienprogramme/braunschweig-projects-deutsch/
 ausschreibung-bewerbung-1?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
URL:https://www.hbk-bs.de/hochschule/stipendienprogramme/braunschweig-proje
 cts-deutsch/ausschreibung-bewerbung-1?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Braunschweig\, Germany. Open internationally (application in Germa
 n or English)\; fellows must reside at HBK for at least 8 months during th
 e lecture periods.
END:VEVENT
