DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261130
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261201
SUMMARY:Deadline: Leibniz Summer Fellowships 2027 (ZZF Potsdam\, contempora
 ry history)
DESCRIPTION:The Leibniz Centre for Contemporary History Potsdam (ZZF) invit
 es applications for two Leibniz Summer Fellowships in German and/or Europe
 an (including Eastern European) history in the twentieth century. Fellows 
 spend two consecutive months between April and October 2027 in Potsdam or 
 Berlin pursuing independent research while taking part in departmental act
 ivities and presenting work in ZZF's research seminar\; the institute's fi
 ve research departments include Contemporary History in the Age of Media a
 nd Information Society. GRANT: EUR 3\,000 per month for two months\, with 
 office space\, computer facilities and specialist library resources. ELIGI
 BILITY: international scholars holding a doctorate and residing outside Ge
 rmany at the time of application. HOW: send a letter of interest\, CV\, pu
 blication list and a research proposal of up to 1\,500 words as a single P
 DF to fellowships@zzf-potsdam.de. DEADLINE: 30 November 2026.\n\nOrganisat
 ion: Leibniz Centre for Contemporary History Potsdam (ZZF)\nLocation: Pots
 dam / Berlin\, Germany. Open to international postdoctoral researchers res
 iding outside Germany.\nAward: Two fellowships of EUR 3\,000 per month for
  two months (EUR 6\,000 total each)\, plus office space\, computer facilit
 ies\, specialist library access and participation in ZZF's academic commun
 ity. No application fee.\nDuration: Two consecutive months between April a
 nd October 2027\n\nMore: https://zzf-potsdam.de/chancen/stellenangebote/le
 ibniz-summer-fellowships-field-german-andor-european-including-eastern?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://zzf-potsdam.de/chancen/stellenangebote/leibniz-summer-fellowshi
 ps-field-german-andor-european-including-eastern?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Potsdam / Berlin\, Germany. Open to international postdoctoral res
 earchers residing outside Germany.
END:VEVENT
