DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:Deadline: Gulbenkian Institute for Advanced Study Fellowships 2027/
 28 (Lisbon)
DESCRIPTION:Residential think-tank fellowships at the Calouste Gulbenkian F
 oundation in Lisbon\, explicitly open to artists as well as academics (aff
 iliated or independent)\, emeritus professors and professionals outside ac
 ademia. Fellows spend 3 to 8 months pursuing self-directed work in any dom
 ain\, provided it needs no laboratory or experimental infrastructure and i
 s not predominantly applied\; selection weighs the CV at 40 percent and th
 e innovativeness of the proposal at 60 percent. WHAT YOU GET: travel\, tra
 vel and health insurance\, a monthly stipend and a partial housing subsidy
 \, with fellow status continuing after the stay. ELIGIBILITY: open interna
 tionally\; past GIAS fellows must wait five years. Applications via the My
 Gulbenkian platform with CV\, a short description of proposed activities a
 nd two referee names. DEADLINE: the annual window runs 1 July to 15 Octobe
 r\; this round closes 15 October 2026 for 2027/28 stays.\n\nOrganisation: 
 Gulbenkian Institute for Advanced Study (GIAS)\, Calouste Gulbenkian Found
 ation\nLocation: Lisbon\, Portugal. Open internationally\; residential fel
 lowships at the Gulbenkian in Lisbon.\nAward: Up to 15 fellowships a year.
  Each covers travel costs\, travel and health insurance\, a monthly stipen
 d and a partial housing subsidy\; the stipend level is set at selection ba
 sed on CV and length of stay. No application fee.\nDuration: 3 to 8 months
  during the 2027/28 academic year\n\nMore: https://gulbenkian.pt/gias/?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://gulbenkian.pt/gias/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_m
 edium=referral
LOCATION:Lisbon\, Portugal. Open internationally\; residential fellowships 
 at the Gulbenkian in Lisbon.
END:VEVENT
