DTSTAMP:20261104T144744Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261127
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261128
SUMMARY:Deadline: DOMA Initiatives x British Council: Venice Biennale Fello
 wship 2027 (Malaysia\, GBP 5\,050)
DESCRIPTION:DOMA Initiatives\, in partnership with the British Council\, no
 minates one Malaysia-based fellow for the British Council Venice Fellowshi
 p Programme at the 2027 Venice Biennale (62nd International Art Exhibition
 ). The fellow spends one month in Venice: half the time as an exhibition a
 mbassador at the British Pavilion (stewarding\, engaging visitors\, suppor
 ting daily gallery operations) and half on independent research or a creat
 ive or architectural project inspired by Venice\, the Pavilion and the Bie
 nnale themes. Fellows complete 15 hours of online training in March-April 
 2027 and\, on return\, run a sharing session\, workshop or exhibition for 
 DOMA Initiatives. ELIGIBILITY: active early-career professionals in archit
 ecture or related creative fields\, based in Malaysia\, with a portfolio i
 ntegrating research or creative practice with the themes of La Biennale di
  Venezia\; strong spoken and written English\; must also meet the British 
 Council criteria in the Venice Fellowship Programme Guidance Notes 2027. H
 OW TO APPLY: complete the application form (Google Doc linked from the cal
 l page) and email it with a CV and portfolio/research proposal to the sele
 ction committee. Shortlisting and interviews 30 November to 3 December 202
 6\; nomination to the British Council 4 December 2026\; final selection an
 nounced January 2027. Contact: Veronica Ng\, DOMA Initiatives Coordinator\
 , veronican@sunway.edu.my. DEADLINE: 27 November 2026\, 12:00 noon MYT.\n\
 nOrganisation: DOMA Initiatives\, in partnership with the British Council\
 nLocation: Venice\, Italy (British Pavilion\, 62nd International Art Exhib
 ition). Only for early-career professionals based in Malaysia.\nAward: GBP
  5\,050 fellowship grant covering travel\, accommodation in Venice\, visa 
 processing and daily living expenses. No separate artist fee or honorarium
  beyond this grant. One fellowship place. No application fee mentioned.\nD
 uration: 1 month in Venice between May and November 2027\, plus 15 hours o
 f online pre-fellowship training in March-April 2027\n\nMore: https://www.
 domainitiatives.org/venice2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_m
 edium=referral
URL:https://www.domainitiatives.org/venice2027?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Venice\, Italy (British Pavilion\, 62nd International Art Exhibiti
 on). Only for early-career professionals based in Malaysia.
END:VEVENT
