SUMMARY:Deadline: ARCAthens: Athens Residency Fellowships (Spring 2027)
DESCRIPTION:The Athens Residency is the flagship program of ARCAthens\, a n
 ot-for-profit founded in 2017\, offering fully funded Fellowships for visu
 al artists and curators to live and work in Athens. The residency is struc
 tured and research-driven\, built around arranged studio and private colle
 ction visits\, institutional access and community events\, balanced with t
 ime for independent work. Fellows take part in one public engagement event
  organized by ARCAthens and must stay based in Athens for the full residen
 cy. ELIGIBILITY: international curators and visual artists residing outsid
 e Greece. SUPPORT: ARCAthens provides housing (private bedroom and bathroo
 m\, shared common spaces)\, travel\, a Fellowship Prize and a weekly stipe
 nd\; Visual Art Fellows get studio access. In the Fall 2026 round this was
  a USD 3\,000 Fellowship Prize plus USD 200 per week. Fellows cover food\,
  local transport and any production or shipping costs\; there is no produc
 tion budget. TIMELINE: applications 16 October to 14 November 2026 (closes
  11:00 p.m. ET)\; notification late November\; residency 4 February to 26 
 April 2027.\n\nOrganisation: ARCAthens\nLocation: Athens\, Greece (in-pers
 on residency). Open to international visual artists and curators residing 
 outside Greece.\nAward: Fully funded: housing\, travel\, a Fellowship Priz
 e and a weekly stipend (most recent published terms\, Fall 2026: USD 3\,00
 0 Fellowship Prize and USD 200/week stipend\, round-trip airfare reimburse
 d). No application fee.\nDuration: About 12 weeks\, 4 February to 26 April
  2027\n\nMore: https://arcathens.org/aa-application/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://arcathens.org/aa-application/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Athens\, Greece (in-person residency). Open to international visua
 l artists and curators residing outside Greece.
END:VEVENT
