SUMMARY:Deadline: Jane Street Graduate Research Fellowship 2027 (tuition pl
 us USD 50\,000 stipend)
DESCRIPTION:Jane Street's Graduate Research Fellowship supports exceptional
  doctoral students in electrical engineering and computer science\, mathem
 atics\, physics or statistics\; research does not need to relate to tradin
 g. ELIGIBILITY: PhD students with at least one year remaining in their pro
 gramme\, or those committed to start a PhD at a specified university in fa
 ll 2027\; fellows must be active full-time PhD students at an accredited r
 esearch institution in the United States\, Canada\, the United Kingdom\, E
 urope\, Australia\, New Zealand or Singapore during the award year. Intern
 ational students are eligible and encouraged. WHAT YOU GET: full tuition a
 nd fees for the upcoming academic year plus a USD 50\,000 stipend (or loca
 l-currency equivalent\; taxable)\; finalists receive USD 5\,000. APPLICATI
 ON: CV\, an optional one-to-two-page research statement and recommender co
 ntact details. DEADLINES: student applications 13 November 2026 AoE\; reco
 mmendation letters 1 December 2026\; notifications in February 2027. Quest
 ions: graduate-research-fellowship@janestreet.com.\n\nOrganisation: Jane S
 treet\nLocation: For full-time PhD students at accredited research institu
 tions in the US\, Canada\, UK\, Europe\, Australia\, New Zealand or Singap
 ore. International students welcome.\nAward: Full tuition and fees for the
  award year plus a USD 50\,000 stipend (or local-currency equivalent\; tax
 able). Finalists receive USD 5\,000. No application fee.\nDuration: One ac
 ademic year.\n\nMore: https://www.janestreet.com/join-jane-street/programs
 -and-events/graduate-research-fellowship/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.janestreet.com/join-jane-street/programs-and-events/graduat
 e-research-fellowship/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
LOCATION:For full-time PhD students at accredited research institutions in 
 the US\, Canada\, UK\, Europe\, Australia\, New Zealand or Singapore. Inte
